From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode <opencode@local>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(follow): speed up live status refresh

Add a lightweight status model so a single request can return live state,
start time and anchor uid without fetching full room details.

- Add LiveStatusInfo plus LiveSite.getLiveStatusInfo with a default
  implementation that falls back to getLiveStatus.
- Bilibili: reuse buvid request, expose uid, add batch status query by uids
  with 99 uid chunking.
- Huya: query the mp.huya.com JSON endpoint first with a 5s timeout and fall
  back to the HTML page.
- Douyu and Douyin: return start time and popularity from the status call.
- HttpClient: allow a per request timeout while keeping the 20s default.
- FollowService: per site concurrency pools, status cache with TTL, single
  flight per room, bounded retry with breaker, incremental re-sort and
  resume refresh.
- Persist last status, last check time, last start time and anchor uid in
  new optional Hive fields.
